              {"number": 2, "prompt": "Stepwells had a range of functions, in addition to those related to water collection.", "answer": "TRUE", "explanation": "Stepwells were places of gathering, leisure, relaxation and worship — beyond water collection.", "evidence": {"sectionId": "p1", "ref": "C", "quote": "they were places of gathering, of leisure, of relaxation and of worship for villagers of all but the lowest castes"}},
              {"number": 3, "prompt": "The few existing stepwells in Delhi are more attractive than those found elsewhere.", "answer": "NOT GIVEN", "explanation": "The passage mentions Delhi stepwells but makes no comparison of their attractiveness.", "evidence": {"sectionId": "p1", "ref": "C", "quote": "a few also survive in Delhi"}},
              {"number": 4, "prompt": "It took workers many years to build the stone steps characteristic of stepwells.", "answer": "NOT GIVEN", "explanation": "The passage gives no information about construction time.", "evidence": {"sectionId": "p1", "ref": "D", "quote": "stepwells comprise a series of stone steps descending from ground level to the water source"}},
              {"number": 5, "prompt": "The number of steps above the water level in a stepwell altered during the course of a year.", "answer": "TRUE", "explanation": "When water was high, fewer steps were descended; when low, several levels had to be negotiated — so exposed steps changed with water level.", "evidence": {"sectionId": "p1", "ref": "D", "quote": "When the water level was high, the user needed only to descend a few steps to reach it; when it was low, several levels would have to be negotiated"}}
