            "instructions": "Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 2? Write TRUE, FALSE, or NOT GIVEN.",
            "questions": [
              {"number": 23, "prompt": "It is likely that the red pigments help to protect the leaf from freezing temperatures.", "answer": "FALSE", "explanation": "Paragraph D says there are 'problems with each of these theories' including freezing tolerance — it is not considered likely.", "evidence": {"sectionId": "p2", "ref": "D", "quote": "there are problems with each of these theories, including the fact that leaves are red for such a relatively short period"}},
              {"number": 24, "prompt": "The 'light screen' hypothesis would initially seem to contradict what is known about chlorophyll.", "answer": "TRUE", "explanation": "Paragraph F states 'It sounds paradoxical' — protecting chlorophyll from light when it is the light absorber seems contradictory.", "evidence": {"sectionId": "p2", "ref": "F", "quote": "It sounds paradoxical, because the idea behind this hypothesis is that the red pigment is made in autumn leaves to protect chlorophyll, the light-absorbing chemical, from too much light"}},
              {"number": 25, "prompt": "Leaves which turn colours other than red are more likely to be damaged by sunlight.", "answer": "NOT GIVEN", "explanation": "Paragraph I acknowledges this is not fully understood but does not claim other-coloured leaves are more easily damaged.", "evidence": {"sectionId": "p2", "ref": "I", "quote": "What is still not fully understood, however, is why some trees resort to producing red pigments while others do not bother"}}
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "multiple_choice",
            "instructions": "Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D.",
            "questions": [
              {"number": 26, "prompt": "For which of the following questions does the writer offer an explanation?", "options": [{"key": "A", "text": "why conifers remain green in winter"}, {"key": "B", "text": "how leaves turn orange and yellow in autumn"}, {"key": "C", "text": "how herbivorous insects choose which trees to lay their eggs in"}, {"key": "D", "text": "why anthocyanins are restricted to certain trees"}], "answer": "B", "explanation": "Paragraph B explicitly explains that orange and yellow are revealed as chlorophyll is depleted ('This unmasking explains the autumn colours of yellow and orange').", "evidence": {"sectionId": "p2", "ref": "B", "quote": "This unmasking explains the autumn colours of yellow and orange"}}
            ]
          }
