            "questions": [
              {"number": 32, "prompt": "According to the writer, there are difficulties explaining how the Lapita accomplished their journeys because", "options": [{"key": "A", "text": "the canoes that have been discovered offer relatively few clues."}, {"key": "B", "text": "archaeologists have shown limited interest in this area of research."}, {"key": "C", "text": "little information relating to this period can be relied upon for accuracy."}, {"key": "D", "text": "technological advances have altered the way such achievements are viewed."}], "answer": "C", "explanation": "No canoes have been found, and oral histories 'turn into myths long before they reach as far back in time as the Lapita' — little reliable information survives.", "evidence": {"sectionId": "p3", "ref": "5", "quote": "Nor do the oral histories and traditions of later Polynesians offer any insights, for they turn into myths long before they reach as far back in time as the Lapita"}},
              {"number": 33, "prompt": "According to the sixth paragraph, what was extraordinary about the Lapita?", "options": [{"key": "A", "text": "They sailed beyond the point where land was visible."}, {"key": "B", "text": "Their cultural heritage discouraged the expression of fear."}, {"key": "C", "text": "They were able to build canoes that withstood ocean voyages."}, {"key": "D", "text": "Their navigational skills were passed on from one generation to the next."}], "answer": "A", "explanation": "'The real adventure did not begin until their Lapita descendants sailed out of sight of land, with empty horizons on every side.'", "evidence": {"sectionId": "p3", "ref": "6", "quote": "The real adventure did not begin, however, until their Lapita descendants sailed out of sight of land, with empty horizons on every side"}},
              {"number": 34, "prompt": "What does 'This' refer to in the seventh paragraph?", "options": [{"key": "A", "text": "the Lapita's seafaring talent"}, {"key": "B", "text": "the Lapita's ability to detect signs of land"}, {"key": "C", "text": "the Lapita's extensive knowledge of the region"}, {"key": "D", "text": "the Lapita's belief they would be able to return home"}], "answer": "D", "explanation": "'This' refers to being 'secure in the knowledge that if they did not find anything, they could turn about and catch a swift ride back' — their confidence in being able to return.", "evidence": {"sectionId": "p3", "ref": "7", "quote": "secure in the knowledge that if they did not find anything, they could turn about and catch a swift ride back on the trade winds. This is what would have made the whole thing work"}},
              {"number": 35, "prompt": "According to the eighth paragraph, how was the geography of the region significant?", "options": [{"key": "A", "text": "It played an important role in Lapita culture."}, {"key": "B", "text": "It meant there were relatively few storms at sea."}, {"key": "C", "text": "It provided a navigational aid for the Lapita."}, {"key": "D", "text": "It made a large number of islands habitable."}], "answer": "C", "explanation": "Vanuatu's chain of intervisible islands formed 'a backstop for mariners riding the trade winds home' — a navigational aid.", "evidence": {"sectionId": "p3", "ref": "8", "quote": "its scores of intervisible islands forming a backstop for mariners riding the trade winds home"}}
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "yes_no_notgiven",
            "instructions": "Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3? Write YES, NO, or NOT GIVEN.",
            "questions": [
              {"number": 36, "prompt": "It is now clear that the Lapita could sail into a prevailing wind.", "answer": "NO", "explanation": "Anderson states 'there is no proof they could do any such thing' — it is not established.", "evidence": {"sectionId": "p3", "ref": "9", "quote": "And there is no proof they could do any such thing"}},
              {"number": 37, "prompt": "Extreme climate conditions may have played a role in Lapita migration.", "answer": "YES", "explanation": "Anderson suggests super El Ninos 'might have taken the Lapita on long unplanned voyages'.", "evidence": {"sectionId": "p3", "ref": "10", "quote": "these super El Ninos might have taken the Lapita on long unplanned voyages"}},
