              {"number": 28, "prompt": "The humpback whale caught off Vancouver Island is mentioned because of", "options": [{"key": "A", "text": "the exceptional size of its body."}, {"key": "B", "text": "the way it exemplifies Dollo's law."}, {"key": "C", "text": "the amount of local controversy it caused."}, {"key": "D", "text": "the reason given for its unusual features."}], "answer": "D", "explanation": "The whale is mentioned because Andrews provided an explanation — it 'must be a throwback to a land-living ancestor'.", "evidence": {"sectionId": "p3", "ref": "4", "quote": "Explorer Roy Chapman Andrews argued at the time that the whale must be a throwback to a land-living ancestor"}},
